From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 20:35:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pstore: add Gemini post-ramoops checkpoint

Add one default-off, experiment-only marker immediately after a ramoops
backend with console storage registers successfully. The marker runs in the
postcore ramoops probe. It precedes built-in DA921x device registration and
gives warm-reset recovery one attributable boundary after kernel entry and
pstore-console availability.

The diagnostic appends one line to the reserved persistent-RAM console. It
performs no device-storage or regulator access. It changes no owner.
CPU8 and CPU9 admission remains closed. This patch uses a synthetic,
non-certifying author identity, carries no sign-off, and is not
submission-ready.
---
 fs/pstore/Kconfig | 13 +++++++++++++
 fs/pstore/ram.c   |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/pstore/Kconfig b/fs/pstore/Kconfig
--- a/fs/pstore/Kconfig
+++ b/fs/pstore/Kconfig
@@ -80,6 +80,19 @@ config PSTORE_RAM
 	  "ramoops.ko".
 
 	  For more information, see Documentation/admin-guide/ramoops.rst.
+
+config PSTORE_GEMINI_POST_RAMOOPS_CHECKPOINT
+	bool "Gemini post-ramoops retained checkpoint"
+	depends on PSTORE_RAM=y
+	depends on PSTORE_CONSOLE && ARM64 && ARCH_MEDIATEK
+	default n
+	help
+	  Emit one attributable persistent-console marker immediately after a
+	  built-in ramoops backend with console storage registers successfully.
+	  This experiment-only diagnostic does not access device storage, read or
+	  write a regulator, change a transition owner, or admit CPU8 or CPU9.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
 
 config PSTORE_ZONE
 	tristate
diff --git a/fs/pstore/ram.c b/fs/pstore/ram.c
--- a/fs/pstore/ram.c
+++ b/fs/pstore/ram.c
@@ -849,8 +849,16 @@ static int ramoops_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	err = pstore_register(&cxt->pstore);
 	if (err) {
 		pr_err("registering with pstore failed\n");
 		goto fail_buf;
 	}
+#ifdef CONFIG_PSTORE_GEMINI_POST_RAMOOPS_CHECKPOINT
+	if (cxt->pstore.flags & PSTORE_FLAGS_CONSOLE)
+		pr_emerg("%s %s %s %s\n",
+			 "GEMINI_MAINLINE_POST_RAMOOPS_20260815_A",
+			 "checkpoint=ramoops-registered pstore_console=active",
+			 "storage_access=none regulator_reads=none",
+			 "regulator_writes=none cpu8_cpu9_admission=closed");
+#endif
 
 	/*
 	 * Update the module parameter variables as well so they are visible
-- 
